==Battleground==
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**12 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 6.67~8 seconds<sup>200f~240f</sup>.
**2 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**2 [[Dagshund]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**2 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**12 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 6.67~8 seconds<sup>200f~240f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The startup enemies in this stage all give decent money, so [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Money Up units]] like [[talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] will be very helpful. Note that the Sir Seals are quite buffed, so taking them down might take a while. The Doge Darks on the other hand, are here solely to give the player money, so they are of no threat.

Upon base hit, a swarm of Brollows, Angelic Gories/Gory Darks, and Professor A. will spawn. [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] can work to fend off the enemies, however support will be necessary. Good units to take out the Professor A. include [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]], especially [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Reds]] such as [[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Once the enemy spam dies down, the stage is won.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Axis of Evil]] stages, Pecking Order has a Russian-themed Japanese name. In this case, Kurimuzon Hiroba (クリムゾン広場) literally translates to "Crimson Plaza" or "Crimson Square", alluding to the [[wikipedia:Red Square|Red Square]] in Moscow.

